      "writtenOn": "2025-04-08T00:21:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since I think this is just going to be a human-facing utility I think it\u0027s fine to just use something other than the official test query, and it\u0027s nice for it to be easy. Your `--test-filter textureSampleLevel` example is definitely compelling. The other issue I have with regex is that a bunch of random stuff will need to be escaped, but fortunately that doesn\u0027t really come up outside of the case parameters, so maybe it doesn\u0027t matter.\n\nI\u0027d still _like_ to use glob (`--test-filter\u003d*textureSampleLevel*`) since it (1) has fewer characters that need escaping and (2) is sorta what we use in expectations, gtest `--test_filter`, etc., except unfortunately I don\u0027t see a builtin implementation in Go. Plus you\u0027d need some way to provide multiple filters like gtest has (whereas regex gets you that for free with `|`).\n\nI\u0027m not opposed to adding some kind of support to standalone/dawn.node, but the wider the scope, the more strongly I think I would prefer glob, even though they\u0027re still all human-facing.\n\nProbably let\u0027s just use regex here for now and if we start adding support in more places then we can standardize on a filter format. Shouldn\u0027t be a big deal to change this later.\n\n(Still nice to have this centralized in GenTestList though!)",
      "parentUuid": "3c8f0747_8b2378d0",
      "revId": "f141d3a3c87c46157e76fbcf418abb62e87d1f2d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
